---
// Timeoff — Cove project page. SCAFFOLD (same system as Cosign).
// 5 demos: full page, hero, four pillars, demo, closing CTA.
// Media are placeholders. Copy = RJ's voice, condensed from the write-up.
const meta = 'Landing Page · Front End · 2026';
const sub = 'Cove — Landing Page';

const beats = [
  [
    "This one came out of an interview process — instead of the usual loop they handed me something better… a brief. Design and build a landing page for Cove, an agentic platform for B2C companies that captures every potential customer interaction, tracks it, and responds — all on its own. I love a good prompt, and I love a time constraint even more. This came to life in roughly 48 hours… have a look.",
    "I'd been dying to do a project with this dithered, pixelated animated look. The organic animations and shapes paired with the dithered effect feel natural yet robotic — perfect for an agentic tool that's supposed to feel like a natural assistant handling the hard parts for you. I started messing with animation in my other tool and landed on these calming animations, then let those lead the direction. Turning chaos into calm.",
  ],
  [
    "The hero is my favorite by far. I knew I wanted a full-bleed animation as the centerpiece, and this distorted flower thing came out so good. The white wordmark in the center took a lot of fiddling — I wanted it subtle and calm, fading in and out of the white that pokes through the animation. A whisper of the company, not a shout.",
    "I like these understated, editorial pages for SaaS because they go against the grain of every other SaaS throwing a million logos, demos, and CTAs at you. It shows up in the quiet nav CTA with a cheeky hover I'm obsessed with, and the footer tagline hinting at more below.",
  ],
  [
    "The four pillars section racked my brain. I had info I needed to share and wasn't sure how to include it tastefully — the typical move is demo after demo and hope the user gets it. I opted for, you guessed it, something simple: plain language of the capabilities on the left, a nice visual on the right. The title text and progress indicators aren't in “traditional” spots, but they add just enough flair. It's also a sticky scroll section, which I typically HATE — the jury's still out on whether I've come around, but it was a fun experiment.",
  ],
  [
    "I'll be honest, the demo section is probably my least favorite… I'm just not a fan of typical demos, they're hard to do right. I had no actual product to base these on, so I went bare bones with a chatbot interface scenario. That said, I enjoy the little scroll journey you're taken on — it serves its purpose well, and I think I executed it fairly well with some fun “pop” animations.",
  ],
  [
    "We skipped the “in your face” CTA in the hero, but this is a SaaS… it has to go somewhere. I like putting them at the end as a bookend, a bit simpler and airy to keep the vibe. This Fraunces-and-Satoshi combo is a homer — it carries the feeling of the closing tagline and CTA. I love when typography does the work for you. Pair that with the same button hover and a gentle floor animation, and you're golden.",
  ],
];
const demoSrcs = ['/cove-full.mp4', '/cove-hero.mp4', '/cove-pillars.mp4', '/cove-demo.mp4', '/cove-cta.mp4'];
const liveUrl = 'https://cove-landing-mock.vercel.app';
const nextProject = { title: 'Stripe Redesign', href: '/stripe-redesign' };
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Cove — Timeoff</title>
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Host+Grotesk:ital,wght@0,400..800;1,400..800&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
    <style>
      :root {
        --ground: #ffffff; --ink: #101113; --ink-soft: #6f6f68; --ink-faint: #a5a49c;
        --placeholder: #ECEBE7; --font: "Host Grotesk", system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
      }
      * { box-sizing: border-box; }
      body { margin: 0; background: var(--ground); color: var(--ink); font-family: var(--font); -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased; text-rendering: optimizeLegibility; }

      .brand {
        position: fixed; top: 1.1rem; left: 50%; transform: translateX(-50%) translateY(0);
        font-size: 0.95rem; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: 0.01em; color: var(--ink);
        text-decoration: none; z-index: 3;
        transition: transform 0.26s cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1), opacity 0.22s ease;
      }
      .brand.tucked { transform: translateX(-50%) translateY(-160%); opacity: 0; pointer-events: none; }
      .back { position: fixed; top: 1.1rem; left: 1.25rem; font-size: 0.95rem; font-weight: 500; color: var(--ink); text-decoration: none; z-index: 3; }
      .back:hover { text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }

      .beats { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 3fr 5fr; column-gap: 2.75rem; row-gap: 6rem; align-items: start; padding: 5.5rem 1.5rem 6rem; max-width: 1600px; margin: 0 auto; }
      .fn { font-size: 0.72rem; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: 0.08em; color: var(--ink-faint); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; margin-bottom: 0.7rem; }
      .beat-text { max-width: 36ch; }
      .proj-title { font-size: 2rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.02em; margin: 0 0 0.3rem; }
      .title-row { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 0.55rem; flex-wrap: wrap; margin: 0 0 0.3rem; }
      .title-row .proj-title { margin: 0; }
      .live-link { font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 500; color: var(--ink-faint); text-decoration: none; display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.2rem; transition: color 0.15s ease; }
      .live-link:hover { color: var(--ink); }
      .live-link svg { width: 0.72em; height: 0.72em; }
      .proj-sub { font-size: 0.98rem; color: var(--ink); margin: 0 0 0.4rem; }
      .proj-meta { font-size: 0.82rem; color: var(--ink-soft); margin: 0 0 1.4rem; }
      .beat-text p { margin: 0; font-size: 0.98rem; line-height: 1.6; }
      .beat-text p + p { margin-top: 1.1rem; }
      .media { aspect-ratio: 1672 / 1080; background: var(--placeholder); border-radius: 2px; width: 100%; overflow: hidden; }
      .media video { width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; display: block; }

      .next { grid-column: 1 / -1; display: inline-flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.3rem; margin-top: 3rem; text-decoration: none; color: inherit; width: max-content; }
      .next-kicker { font-size: 0.72rem; letter-spacing: 0.08em; color: var(--ink-faint); }
      .next-title { font-size: 1.6rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.02em; transition: transform 0.4s cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.7, 0.2, 1); }
      .next:hover .next-title { transform: translateX(0.4rem); }

      .beat-text, .beat-media, .next {
        opacity: 0; transform: translateY(14px);
        animation: rise 0.6s cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.7, 0.2, 1) forwards; animation-delay: calc(var(--i) * 90ms);
      }
      @keyframes rise { to { opacity: 1; transform: none; } }
      @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
        .beat-text, .beat-media, .next { opacity: 1; transform: none; animation: none; }
        .brand { transition: opacity 0.3s ease; }
        .brand.tucked { transform: translateX(-50%) translateY(0); }
      }
      @media (max-width: 900px) { .beats { grid-template-columns: 1fr; row-gap: 2.5rem; } .beat-text { max-width: none; } }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <a class="back" href="/work">Work</a>
    <a class="brand" href="/">timeoff</a>

    <main class="beats">
      {beats.map((paras, i) => (
        <>
          <div class="beat-text" style={`--i:${i}`}>
            <div class="fn">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</div>
            {i === 0 && (
              <div class="title-row">
                <h1 class="proj-title">Cove</h1>
                <a class="live-link" href={liveUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Live<svg viewBox="0 0 12 12" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 9L9 3M9 3H4M9 3V8" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
              </div>
            )}
            {i === 0 && <p class="proj-sub">{sub}</p>}
            {i === 0 && <p class="proj-meta">{meta}</p>}
            {paras.map((para) => <p>{para}</p>)}
          </div>
          <div class="beat-media" style={`--i:${i}`}>
            <div class="fn">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</div>
            <div class="media">
              <video class="demo" src={demoSrcs[i]} muted loop playsinline preload="metadata"></video>
            </div>
          </div>
        </>
      ))}

      <a class="next" href={nextProject.href}>
        <span class="next-kicker">Next</span>
        <span class="next-title">{nextProject.title}</span>
      </a>
    </main>

    <script is:inline>
      (function () {
        var brand = document.querySelector('.brand');
        if (!brand) return;
        var THRESHOLD = 6, ticking = false;
        function update() { brand.classList.toggle('tucked', window.scrollY > THRESHOLD); ticking = false; }
        window.addEventListener('scroll', function () { if (!ticking) { window.requestAnimationFrame(update); ticking = true; } }, { passive: true });
        update();
      })();

      // demo videos play only while in view (muted, looping)
      (function () {
        var vids = document.querySelectorAll('video.demo');
        if (!vids.length || !('IntersectionObserver' in window)) return;
        var io = new IntersectionObserver(function (entries) {
          entries.forEach(function (en) {
            if (en.isIntersecting) { var p = en.target.play(); if (p && p.catch) p.catch(function () {}); }
            else { en.target.pause(); }
          });
        }, { threshold: 0.4 });
        vids.forEach(function (v) { io.observe(v); });
      })();
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
